@startuml
title Option C — Cloudflare Access to Supabase JWT bridge
autonumber

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #202124
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2F5D8A
  LifeLineBorderColor #8A8A8A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #2F5D8A
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF2FA
  ParticipantFontColor #202124
  ActorBorderColor #2F5D8A
  ActorBackgroundColor #EAF2FA
  ActorFontColor #202124
  GroupBorderColor #8A8A8A
  GroupBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
  GroupFontColor #202124
}

actor Client
participant "Cloudflare Access" as Access
participant "Worker\nitems-api-worker" as Worker
collections "Cloudflare Access JWKS" as AccessJWKS
database "Worker secret\nES256 private JWK" as WorkerKey
participant "Supabase Data API\n(PostgREST)" as DataAPI
collections "Supabase signing keys\n(public JWK set)" as SupabaseKeys
database "Postgres + RLS" as DB

Client -> Access: GET /items

alt No valid Access session
  Access -> Client: Access login / identity-provider redirect
  Client -> Access: completes login
end

Access -> Worker: GET /items\nCf-Access-Jwt-Assertion: <Access JWT>
note right of Worker
The client never provides a Supabase JWT
to the Option C Worker.
end note

Worker -> AccessJWKS: fetch or use cached JWKS
AccessJWKS --> Worker: public Access signing keys
Worker -> Worker: jwtVerify(assertion)\nrequire expected issuer + application aud

alt Missing, invalid, expired, wrong issuer, or wrong aud
  Worker --> Client: 403 Cloudflare Access authentication required/invalid
else Valid Access assertion
  Worker -> Worker: read identity: sub + email
  Worker -> Worker: reject if sub is not UUID-shaped
  Worker -> WorkerKey: import ES256 private JWK
  Worker -> Worker: mint bridge JWT\nheader: alg=ES256, kid=<imported key kid>\nclaims: sub, email, cf_access_sub,\nrole=authenticated, iat, exp=now+300s
  Worker -> DataAPI: CRUD request\napikey: <publishable key>\nAuthorization: Bearer <bridge JWT>
  DataAPI -> SupabaseKeys: select trusted signing key by kid\nverify ES256 signature

  alt JWT invalid, unknown kid, bad signature, or expired
    DataAPI --> Worker: 401 JWT rejected
    Worker --> Client: error response
  else Bridge JWT trusted
    DataAPI -> DB: SET request.jwt.claims\nexecute query as authenticated
    DB -> DB: auth.uid() = JWT sub\nRLS evaluates authenticated policies

    alt RLS allows request
      DB --> DataAPI: allowed rows / mutation result
      DataAPI --> Worker: success payload
      Worker --> Client: success payload
    else RLS denies request
      DB --> DataAPI: empty result or RLS error
      DataAPI --> Worker: denied result
      Worker --> Client: result/error
    end
  end
end

note over Access,DB
GoTrue remains enabled. Its existing Supabase Auth JWT path remains separate
while Access-sub to existing user_id migration/mapping is deliberately deferred.
end note
@enduml
